WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.190
One of the things I turn to

2
00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:04.730
when I'm going through the hardest stuff,

3
00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:08.580
for me was self-soothing coping mechanisms.

4
00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:10.980
How do I not feel this?

5
00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:12.580
How do I

6
00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:14.980
numb?

7
00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:17.960
How do I even like, actually feel really good?

8
00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:20.610
That's the thing is like, who doesn't wanna feel good?

9
00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:23.490
Like feeling good is,

10
00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:26.260 line:15%
feels good and feeling bad, feels bad.

11
00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:28.220 line:15%
And that's the big, and like,

12
00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:30.410 line:15%
that's one of the things

13
00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:32.070
that I think,

14
00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:34.530
you know, jumping right into it with no shame,

15
00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:37.230
like I've been very open about the fact that, you know,

16
00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:38.430
toward the end of my illness

17
00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:42.630
I developed a serious addiction to benzodiazepines,

18
00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:43.463
to Klonopin.

19
00:00:43.463 --> 00:00:46.190
Like I was addicted to antianxiety medication.

20
00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:49.010
I was a good old fashioned pill head.

21
00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:51.520
I was like, that is what I like to call it

22
00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:54.220
because I don't think

23
00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:56.870
that there needs to be a cute word for it,

24
00:00:56.870 --> 00:01:00.260
because I don't think that we should have shame.

25
00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:02.910
It's like, if you think about it

26
00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:05.730
feeling bad feels bad, feeling good feels good.

27
00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:09.520
No one should be ashamed about wanting to get out of pain.

28
00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:11.510
And what addiction is,

29
00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:14.060
is like a desire to get out of pain

30
00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:17.310
and not having the tools to get out of pain.

31
00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:20.170
And almost no one is given the proper tools

32
00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:22.303
by their parents, by their teachers,

33
00:01:23.304 --> 00:01:26.410
by the infrastructure of this country

34
00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:30.690
and how we deal with mental health to get out of pain.

35
00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:34.100
And I was really lucky I have an amazing family.

36
00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:36.460
I've been in therapy since I was a kid

37
00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:39.790
but somewhere along the path of my twenties

38
00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:41.810
the way that my career swept me up,

39
00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:43.360
what I thought the expectations

40
00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:45.720
or what I thought the expectations were

41
00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:47.060
the way that people were looking at me

42
00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:49.120
how I thought I had to perform.

43
00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:50.970
I just remember being so terrified

44
00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:52.450
of the idea of disappointing people

45
00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:53.900
that really for me at first,

46
00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:56.170
I was like if I can take these drugs

47
00:01:56.170 --> 00:01:57.920
and they make me more like myself,

48
00:01:57.920 --> 00:01:59.830
isn't that a better thing?

49
00:01:59.830 --> 00:02:02.020
And then suddenly I realized I was becoming less

50
00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:03.410
and less like myself.

51
00:02:03.410 --> 00:02:07.340
And suddenly it was like sobriety wasn't a choice for me

52
00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:08.610
I was thrust into it,

53
00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:11.390
because I realized there was no other way

54
00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:15.410
that I was going to get back to the life that I loved.

55
00:02:15.410 --> 00:02:17.200
And so, in a way it was

56
00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:19.350
I love to think it was this very Zen Choice.

57
00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:20.183
Like, you know what,

58
00:02:20.183 --> 00:02:21.690
I think I'm just gonna have a dry January

59
00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:23.728
and then it turned into a dry,

60
00:02:23.728 --> 00:02:28.470
but no, it was like, girl, you gotta get it together.

61
00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:30.930
And then, but it turned out to be like

62
00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:32.620
the greatest thing I ever did.

63
00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:35.883
Like I'm almost three years out.

64
00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:38.690
I feel blessed that

65
00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:40.930
it's not something that I don't sit around every day

66
00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:43.580
wishing I had like a high ball in my hand or something.

67
00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:46.180
I am the greatest friends

68
00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:48.310
of my life have come out of sobriety.

69
00:02:48.310 --> 00:02:49.270
That's not to say

70
00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:51.030 line:15%
that life is perfect every day

71
00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:53.310 line:15%
but it's almost like I compare it to like

72
00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:55.280 line:15%
in sobriety you're building this,

73
00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:57.820
your life is like this boat and you're building this boat

74
00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:01.260
and it's not that issues don't come along

75
00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:03.360
but it's like the boats just kind of floating

76
00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:05.330
on nice water and then you're testing it.

77
00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:07.010
And you're seeing like, does it actually work?

78
00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:09.580
And then like a huge wave comes along and you're like

79
00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:11.010
Oh crap, that didn't sink.

80
00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:12.820
Like we built a pretty good boat.

81
00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:17.290
And I feel that way, every time something big or scary

82
00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:18.640
or challenging comes along sobriety.

83
00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:19.810
I'm like that boat's,

84
00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:22.420
that boat still up, that boots still bobbing.

85
00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:23.840
The boat, perfect.

86
00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:25.384
The wave, I get it.

87
00:03:25.384 --> 00:03:27.210
I so get it.

88
00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:30.993
Did you have the voice of, I know this is not working.

89
00:03:32.533 --> 00:03:34.370
I'm sabotaging.

90
00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:35.330
I'm not healthy.

91
00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:36.950
I'm not well,

92
00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:37.783
but shh.

93
00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:39.743
I'm gonna fix it.

94
00:03:39.743 --> 00:03:41.950
I'll get through the day, just shut up voices.

95
00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:44.220
I know what you're telling me.

96
00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:46.460
I hear you, but I'm not listening,

97
00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:50.933
or was it denial and then the aha moment, which path?

98
00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:54.370
100%, the first one you're describing,

99
00:03:54.370 --> 00:03:57.210
like especially when I would lay down in bed at night

100
00:03:57.210 --> 00:04:01.910
it would just be like, this is a disaster.

101
00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:03.440
And you know I regret,

102
00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:05.230
in a certain way I regret nothing.

103
00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:06.900
The only things I regret in life

104
00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:09.330
are the moments that I've hurt people.

105
00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:11.370
I think all the moments that I've hurt myself

106
00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:16.160
were probably pretty educational to be frank.

107
00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:20.120
I had times in my life where I think,

108
00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:24.670
you know maybe there's the on top of the world

109
00:04:24.670 --> 00:04:25.503
and then

110
00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:28.630
as you were

111
00:04:28.630 --> 00:04:31.370
and whether it's subconscious or conscious

112
00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:34.800
I guess that is the question you have burn it all down.

113
00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.180
I have a really interesting

114
00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:38.010
as I'm sure many of us do relationship

115
00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:40.630
between the people pleaser in me and the rebel in me

116
00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:43.820
who are always doing a dance with each other.

117
00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:48.600
And I think you may enjoy a little bit of that too.

118
00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:51.670
I see you grooving to the same song.

119
00:04:51.670 --> 00:04:54.090
And so I think there was a part of me that was like

120
00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:57.710
I don't know how to get out of this phase of my life.

121
00:04:57.710 --> 00:05:01.390
I only know how to like pull the rip cord.

122
00:05:01.390 --> 00:05:03.640
And I'm not saying anyone should feel sorry for me for that.

123
00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:04.879
It just is the truth.

124
00:05:04.879 --> 00:05:07.546
(upbeat music)

